** Opener after a response and an overcall

Phase 4 replaces the natural fallback of NOTES.md #C4 at the most frequent of
these positions (a one-level response, then a suit overcall, 1NT or a double
by opener's left-hand opponent): opener raises responder's suit with four-card
support at the cheapest level with 12--15, a level higher with 16--18 (game
in a major with 19+), rebids a six-card suit with 12--16, bids 1NT with 12--14
balanced and a stopper when it is still available, and otherwise passes.
Responder then passes.

